data.reasoningText:
Now I have a good understanding of the project structure. Let me plan and implement the chat page.

## Component Plan: Team Messaging Chat

### Component Tree
```
ChatPage                    (page — owns all state, orchestrates layout)
├── ChannelSidebar          (channel list with active selection)
│   └── ChannelItem         (single channel: name, desc, unread badge)
├── MessageArea             (main message panel)
│   ├── MessageBubble       (single message with reactions, hover actions)
│   └── MessageInput        (textarea + send button, reused in thread)
└── ThreadPanel             (collapsible right panel for thread replies)
```

The data flows from ChatPage down to each section — it manages the channels, selected channel, messages, and thread state, then passes relevant data and callbacks to the sidebar, message area, and thread panel. MessageInput gets reused in both the main message area and the thread panel for consistency.

I'm planning the implementation order starting with the service contracts and models, then building up from leaf components like ChannelItem and MessageBubble, through the reusable MessageInput, and finally the container components like MessageArea and ThreadPanel, with ChatPage tying everything together. I'll organize the chat components under a Components/Chat folder and use the root namespace for the project structure.

```

csharp
// Services/ChatModels.cs
public record Channel(string Id, string Name);
public record Message(string Id, string Content, string Author, DateTime Timestamp);
public record Thread(string Id, List<Message> Messages);

public interface IChatService
{
    Task<List<Channel>> GetChannelsAsync();
    Task<List<Message>> GetMessagesAsync(string channelId);
    Task SendMessageAsync(string channelId, string content);
}
```

Now I'll create the Razor components starting with the leaf components and working up to the page.

For ChannelItem.razor, I'll create a simple component that displays a channel name and handles click events to select it.

For ChannelSidebar.razor, I'll render a list of channels using the ChannelItem component and manage which channel is currently selected.

For MessageBubble.razor, I'll display individual messages with the author name, timestamp, and content.

For MessageInput.razor, I'll create a text input field with a send button that calls the chat service.

For MessageArea.razor, I'll combine the message bubbles and input component to show the conversation.

For ThreadPanel.razor, I'll display thread replies in a side panel when a message with replies is selected.

Finally, Chat.razor will be the main page that orchestrates all these components, manages the selected channel and messages, and injects the IChatService.

I need to think about state management - the page will need to track the current channel, messages, and selected message for threading. I'll use component parameters and cascading parameters to pass data down and event callbacks to communicate up.

For styling, I'll use scoped CSS files for each component to keep styles isolated and maintainable.

Let me start building these components now.

Actually, I realize I need to think about the thread functionality more carefully. The service has a `GetThreadAsync` method that takes a root message ID, but I need to figure out which messages are thread starters. Looking at the data model, messages can have a `ReplyToId` field. So a message is a thread starter if other messages reference it as their `ReplyToId`. I'll need to track this on the client side when loading messages - I can check which messages are referenced as replies and mark those as having threads.

I think the cleanest approach is to load all messages for a channel, then on the client side, identify which messages have replies by checking if any other message has that message's ID as its `ReplyToId`. Then when the user clicks on a message with replies, I'll call `GetThreadAsync` to load the full thread.

Let me start implementing the components now.

I'll create the ChannelItem component first - it's the simplest and doesn't depend on other components.

```csharp
// Components/Chat/ChannelItem.razor
@if (Channel != null)
{
    <div class="channel-item @(IsSelected ? "selected" : "")" @onclick="OnClick">
        <span>@Channel.Name</span>
    </div>
}

@code {
    [Parameter]
    public Channel Channel { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public bool IsSelected { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback OnSelect { get; set; }

    private async Task OnClick()
    {
        await OnSelect.InvokeAsync();
    }
}
```

Now for ChannelSidebar.razor:

```csharp
// Components/Chat/ChannelSidebar.razor
<div class="channel-sidebar">
    @if (Channels != null)
    {
        @foreach (var channel in Channels)
        {
            <ChannelItem 
                Channel="channel" 
                IsSelected="SelectedChannelId == channel.Id"
                OnSelect="@(() => OnChannelSelect.InvokeAsync(channel.Id))" />
        }
    }
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter]
    public List<Channel> Channels { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string SelectedChannelId { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string> OnChannelSelect { get; set; }
}
```

For MessageBubble.razor:

```csharp
// Components/Chat/MessageBubble.razor
<div class="message-bubble @(IsOwn ? "own" : "other")">
    <div class="message-header">
        <span class="author">@Message.Author</span>
        <span class="timestamp">@Message.Timestamp.ToString("HH:mm")</span>
    </div>
    <div class="message-content">@Message.Content</div>
    @if (HasReplies)
    {
        <div class="thread-indicator" @onclick="OnThreadClick">
            <span>@ReplyCount replies</span>
        </div>
    }
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter]
    public Message Message { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public bool IsOwn { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public bool HasReplies { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public int ReplyCount { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback OnThreadClick { get; set; }

    private async Task OnThreadClick()
    {
        await OnThreadClick.InvokeAsync();
    }
}
```

For MessageInput.razor:

```csharp
// Components/Chat/MessageInput.razor
<div class="message-input-container">
    <input 
        type="text" 
        placeholder="Type a message..." 
        @bind="messageText"
        @onkeyup="HandleKeyUp" />
    <button @onclick="SendMessage">Send</button>
</div>

@code {
    private string messageText = "";

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string> OnSendMessage { get; set; }

    private async Task SendMessage()
    {
        if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(messageText))
        {
            await OnSendMessage.InvokeAsync(messageText);
            messageText = "";
        }
    }

    private async Task HandleKeyUp(KeyboardEventArgs e)
    {
        if (e.Key == "Enter")
        {
            await SendMessage();
        }
    }
}
```

For MessageArea.razor:

```csharp
// Components/Chat/MessageArea.razor
<div class="message-area">
    @if (Messages != null)
    {
        @foreach (var message in Messages)
        {
            <MessageBubble 
                Message="message"
                IsOwn="message.Author == CurrentUser"
                HasReplies="ThreadSummaries.ContainsKey(message.Id)"
                ReplyCount="ThreadSummaries.ContainsKey(message.Id) ? ThreadSummaries[message.Id].ReplyCount : 0"
                OnThreadClick="@(() => OnThreadSelect.InvokeAsync(message.Id))" />
        }
    }
    <MessageInput OnSendMessage="OnSendMessage" />
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter]
    public List<Message> Messages { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string CurrentUser { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public Dictionary<int, ThreadSummary> ThreadSummaries { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<int> OnThreadSelect { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string> OnSendMessage { get; set; }
}
```

For ThreadPanel.razor:

```csharp
// Components/Chat/ThreadPanel.razor
@if (Thread != null && Thread.Any())
{
    <div class="thread-panel">
        <div class="thread-header">
            <h3>Thread</h3>
            <button @onclick="OnClose">Close</button>
        </div>
        <div class="thread-messages">
            @foreach (var message in Thread)
            {
                <MessageBubble 
                    Message="message"
                    IsOwn="message.Author == CurrentUser"
                    HasReplies="false" />
            }
        </div>
        <MessageInput OnSendMessage="OnSendReply" />
    </div>
}

@code {
    [Parameter]
    public List<Message> Thread { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string CurrentUser { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback OnClose { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string> OnSendReply { get; set; }
}
```

Finally, for Chat.razor:

```csharp
// Pages/Chat.razor
@page "/chat"
@inject IChatService ChatService

<div class="chat-container">
    <ChannelSidebar 
        Channels="channels"
        SelectedChannelId="selectedChannelId"
        OnChannelSelect="SelectChannel" />

    <MessageArea 
        Messages="messages"
        CurrentUser="currentUser"
        ThreadSummaries="threadSummaries"
        OnThreadSelect="SelectThread"
        OnSendMessage="SendMessage" />

    @if (selectedThreadId.HasValue)
    {
        <ThreadPanel 
            Thread="threadMessages"
            CurrentUser="currentUser"
            OnClose="CloseThread"
            OnSendReply="SendThreadReply" />
    }
</div>

@code {
    private List<Channel> channels = new();
    private List<Message> messages = new();
    private List<Message> threadMessages = new();
    private Dictionary<int, ThreadSummary> threadSummaries = new();

    private int selectedChannelId;
    private int? selectedThreadId;
    private string currentUser = "CurrentUser";

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        channels = await ChatService.GetChannelsAsync();
        if (channels.Any())
        {
            await SelectChannel(channels.First().Id);
        }
    }

    private async Task SelectChannel(int channelId)
    {
        selectedChannelId = channelId;
        selectedThreadId = null;
        messages = await ChatService.GetMessagesAsync(channelId, 0, 50);

        // Load thread summaries for messages that are thread starters
        foreach (var message in messages)
        {
            var thread = await ChatService.GetThreadAsync(message.Id);
            if (thread.Count > 0)
            {
                threadSummaries[message.Id] = new ThreadSummary(
                    message.Id,
                    thread.Count,
                    thread.Max(m => m.SentAt)
                );
            }
        }
    }

    private async Task SelectThread(int rootMessageId)
    {
        selectedThreadId = rootMessageId;
        threadMessages = await ChatService.GetThreadAsync(rootMessageId);
    }

    private void CloseThread()
    {
        selectedThreadId = null;
        threadMessages.Clear();
    }

    private async Task SendMessage(string content)
    {
        var message = await ChatService.SendMessageAsync(selectedChannelId, content, null);
        messages.Add(message);
    }

    private async Task SendThreadReply(string content)
    {
        if (selectedThreadId.HasValue)
        {
            var message = await ChatService.SendMessageAsync(selectedChannelId, content, selectedThreadId.Value);
            threadMessages.Add(message);
        }
    }
}
```

For the CSS, I'll create Chat.razor.css:

